{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792490173,"nonce":"QWVNClKDoygVQQGimKma8T3qJXw=","message":"Looked at the DILocation part. The module's IR is already released after the code loads (release_module_ir removes it from the engine once attach_loaded has copied the rows), so what stays is the DILocation nodes themselves: LLVM keeps uniqued metadata for the life of its LLVMContext, and ash uses one context for every module, so stripping the module's debug info does not free them. They number one per distinct (frame chain, function), the 74,734 blocks, 4.6 MB of the 25. Freeing them needs the metadata in a context that can be destroyed after the load, i.e. a context per promoted module, which means the lowering state tied to the shared context (cached types, declarations) would have to be per module; not a small change for 4.6 MB. The other items are not metadata: raw_svector_ostream (2.7 MB) is the object file MCJIT keeps for each loaded module, set_positions and attach_loaded (4.2 MB) are the trace position tables that backtraces read, and the air and cranelift data (about 9 MB) are untouched until re-tiering and OSR re-entry are checked. No change made.","files":null}]}